        "id": "stage-9-topic-5-section-4",
        "title": "Docker Authentication — Image Tagging and Digest Management",
        "content": "## Docker Authentication — Image Tagging and Digest Management\n\n### Core technical explanation\n\nDocker authentication allows a local Docker client or CI runner to establish an authenticated session with a private ECR registry. The AWS CLI obtains an authorization token using the current AWS identity. The standard login workflow uses aws ecr get-login-password for the repository Region and pipes the token to docker login with username AWS and password-stdin. The registry hostname must match the account and Region that own the repository. Use password-stdin so the token is not exposed as a command-line argument. In CI, prefer short-lived credentials obtained through an IAM role or federation rather than permanent access keys stored in source code. Authentication confirms the identity to the registry; it does not automatically grant permission to every repository. IAM and repository policies still determine whether the principal can push or pull. If login succeeds but a push fails, inspect repository permissions and the image reference. If login itself fails, inspect AWS credentials, token retrieval, Region selection, network connectivity, and the registry endpoint. Never print authorization tokens in pipeline logs.\n\n### Section-specific learning objective\n\nExplain credential retrieval, token handling, Docker login, Region selection, token lifetime, secure CI usage, and the distinction between authentication and authorization.\n\n### Practical implementation and commands\n\nThe following commands demonstrate the relevant ECR workflow. Replace ACCOUNT_ID, ROLE_NAME, repository names, image tags, and Region with values from the target AWS environment. Review the target resource and permissions before running configuration-changing commands.\n\naws ecr get-login-password --region ap-south-1 | docker login --username AWS --password-stdin ACCOUNT_ID.dkr.ecr.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com\n\n### CI/CD integration\n\nIn a production pipeline, use a dedic